We need answer physics multiple choice. Need solve. Solar flux 1000 W/m^2, normal to completely reflecting surface area 3 m^2. Radiation pressure for perfect reflector normal incidence: P = 2I/c. Force = P A = 2 I A / c. I=1000, A=3, c=3e8. F=2*1000*3/3e8 = 6000/3e8 = 2e-5 N. Option C. Need final with Answer: C. Ensure maybe if completely reflecting surface, momentum change double. Yes.
</think>

The radiation force on a perfectly reflecting surface is

\[
F = \frac{2IA}{c}
\]

where \(I = 1000\ \text{W/m}^2\), \(A = 3\ \text{m}^2\), and \(c \approx 3 \times 10^8\ \text{m/s}\).

\[
F = \frac{2(1000)(3)}{3 \times 10^8}
= \frac{6000}{3 \times 10^8}
= 2 \times 10^{-5}\ \text{N}
\]

